"The Yellow Emperor's Inner Classic, one of the oldest texts in Chinese medicine, states the idea in four characters: overexertion drains qi. The same chapter goes even further, claiming that a hundred diseases arise from qi. What makes this idea useful today is what counts as \"overexertion.\" It is not limited to physical labor. Thinking too much, carrying responsibility for too long, and never quite letting go of a worry are all treated as forms of overexertion in Chinese medicine — the same category as working a double shift.": "eb1a972a94b5",
